{
  "info": {
    "name": "Acento — API Franquicias",
    "description": "Coleccion para probar la API de Acento de punta a punta.\n\nUso:\n1. Importar este archivo en Postman (o correr con Newman).\n2. Ejecutar las carpetas EN ORDEN: Seguridad -> Auth -> Usuarios -> Franquicias -> Sucursales -> Productos -> Limpieza.\n3. El script de pre-request de la coleccion pide /auth/csrf y copia el token a la cabecera X-XSRF-TOKEN; Postman guarda las cookies solo.\n\nOrden importante: el registro va al final porque inicia sesion como el usuario nuevo y dejaria sin permisos de ADMIN al resto de la corrida.\n\nAntes de correr: completar las variables adminEmail, adminPassword y userPassword con los valores del .env de la raiz.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "host", "value": "https://prueba-accenture.com" },
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "https://prueba-accenture.com/api/v1" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userPassword", "value": "" },
    { "key": "fid", "value": "" },
    { "key": "bid", "value": "" },
    { "key": "pid", "value": "" },
    { "key": "uid", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Double submit cookie. En pre-request la URL aun no esta interpolada",
          "// ({{baseUrl}}), asi que pm.cookies.get no ve nada: el token se guarda en",
          "// una variable de coleccion al pedir /auth/csrf.",
          "const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('csrfToken');",
          "if (token) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-XSRF-TOKEN', value: token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Seguridad (sin sesion)",
      "description": "Rutas no declaradas y acceso sin sesion. Va primero porque necesita el cookie jar vacio.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. GET ruta inexistente sin sesion",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('401 sin sesion', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{host}}/api/v2/inexistente",
              "host": ["{{host}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v2", "inexistente"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Sesion por cookie HttpOnly + CSRF de doble cookie.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2. GET /auth/csrf",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('204 y guarda el token CSRF', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "  const token = pm.cookies.get('XSRF-TOKEN');",
                  "  pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', token);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "csrf"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. POST /auth/login (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 con rol ADMIN', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().roles).to.include('ADMIN');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. GET /auth/me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 con la sesion', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().email).to.eql(pm.variables.get('adminEmail'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. POST /auth/login (contrasena incorrecta)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"incorrecta1!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
